WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.310
Picture two food trucks
parked side by side.

2
00:00:03.310 --> 00:00:08.010
On Monday, both raise every
price on the menu by 10 percent.

3
00:00:08.010 --> 00:00:12.010
By Friday, one truck has taken
in more money than last week.

4
00:00:12.010 --> 00:00:14.350
The other has taken in less.

5
00:00:14.350 --> 00:00:16.720
So when a seller charges more,

6
00:00:16.720 --> 00:00:19.390
why does the money
coming in sometimes go up

7
00:00:19.390 --> 00:00:21.350
and sometimes go down?

8
00:00:21.350 --> 00:00:24.450
In this mission, you'll
run the total revenue test,

9
00:00:24.450 --> 00:00:27.850
the quick check economists
use to read a price change.

10
00:00:27.850 --> 00:00:31.300
Then you'll travel down a
straight-line demand curve and track

11
00:00:31.300 --> 00:00:33.840
total revenue at every price.

12
00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:38.030
Your mission: explain what
decides which way the money moves.
